NNAAMMEE
     wwccwwiiddtthh — number of column positions of a wide-character code

LLIIBBRRAARRYY
     Standard C Library (libc, -lc)

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ##iinncclluuddee <<wwcchhaarr..hh>>

     _i_n_t
     wwccwwiiddtthh(_w_c_h_a_r___t _w_c);

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The wwccwwiiddtthh() function determines the number of column positions required
     to display the wide character _w_c.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The wwccwwiiddtthh() function returns 0 if the _w_c argument is a null wide char‐
     acter (L'\0'), -1 if _w_c is not printable, otherwise it returns the number
     of column positions the character occupies.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     This code fragment reads text from standard input and breaks lines that
     are more than 20 column positions wide, similar to the fold(1) utility:

           wint_t ch;
           int column, w;

           column = 0;
           while ((ch = getwchar()) != WEOF) {
                   w = wcwidth(ch);
                   if (w > 0 && column + w >= 20) {
                           putwchar(L'\n');
                           column = 0;
                   }
                   putwchar(ch);
                   if (ch == L'\n')
                           column = 0;
                   else if (w > 0)
                           column += w;
           }

